In the triangle shown, $n$ is a positive integer, and $\angle A > \angle B > \angle C$.  How many possible values of $n$ are there? [asy]
draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(.4,.5)--cycle);
label("$A$",(.4,.5),N); label("$B$",(1,0),SE); label("$C$",(0,0),SW);
label("$2n + 12$",(.5,0),S); label("$3n - 3$",(.7,.25),NE); label("$2n + 7$",(.2,.25),NW);
[/asy]

A referendum failed by a vote of 36 No's and 24 Yes's. To make this pie chart of this result, what is the lesser measure in degrees of angle $ACB$?

[asy]
import graph;
draw(Circle((0,0),20));
draw((0,0)--(0,20));
draw((0,0)--(12,-16));
label("$A$",(0,20),N);
label("$B$",(12,-16),SE);
label("$C$",(0,0),W);
label("YES",(10,13),S);
label("NO",(-10,13),S);
label("36",(-10,10),S);
label("24",(10,10),S);
[/asy]
